<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Archidona</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Archidona is a town in the province of Málaga in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andalusia">Andalusia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, below a hill crowned by the remains of a Moorish fortress. Under the Nasrid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a> it was an important frontier stronghold on the north-western approaches to Granada, and it fell to Castilian forces in 1462, the same year <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gibraltar">Gibraltar</a> was lost. Its octagonal main square dates from the eighteenth century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/archidona.jpg" alt="Archidona" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ingo Mehling · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Archidona_View.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
